mode: "100644"
text: "# Social selling & DMs 2026 — verified\n\n*Volatile. Re-verify quarterly (Meta DM rules + limits change often).*\n\n## The shift: feed → inbox (but only on permission)\nFeed engagement fell from ~2.94% (2024) to **<1% (2026)** while **DM open rates sit at 88–90%** — \"the\nopportunity moved from public feeds to private conversations.\" But it works **one way only**: as a\n**response to intent** (someone commented, replied to a Story, followed, or sent a keyword), **never as\ncold outreach.** The test: *did the user ask for this through an explicit action?* If yes → fine. If no →\nspam. **Permission is the whole game.**\n\n## Warm vs cold (the risk axis)\n**Warm** (commented / followed / replied / previously messaged) = low risk; the platform reads it as\ncontinuing a conversation they started. **Cold** (no relationship) = highest spam risk and **where most\nbans originate.** Above ~50 DMs/day, cold outreach is simply the wrong approach.\n\n## Why it converts\nSpeed compounds — classic lead-response research puts a **~1-minute reply at ~391% better conversion**\nthan a 30-minute wait, and the same decay applies in the inbox. **Micro-accounts (1K–50K) convert\n15–20%** DM-to-sale (vs 7–10% larger) — smaller, more engaged audiences respond more. Personalized\noutreach ~32% response vs ~18% cold email.\n\n## The comment → DM → email funnel (the canonical 2026 play)\nCaption a Reel/carousel \"**Comment KEYWORD and I'll DM you the free [magnet]**\" → follower comments →\na **warm DM delivers the value** → **capture the email natively in the chat** → soft next step while\nwarm. Public comments = social proof + a strong engagement signal + a natural bridge public→private. Five\nflows: comment-to-DM, story-reply, keyword-triggered, welcome DM, re-engagement.\n\n## Meta's rules (May 2026) — official API only\n**Allowed:** automated replies to comments/story-replies/keyword DMs **via the official Meta API**; links/\nmedia in DMs; collecting email in DM; follow-up **within the 24-hour window**; tools on the official API\n(ManyChat, LinkDM, CreatorFlow, PilotDM…). **Not allowed:** DMs to people who haven't interacted (cold\nvia API); exceeding pacing caps (~200/hr tool-side); messaging **outside the 24h window** without a new\ninteraction; **unofficial/scraping/password tools**; misleading/spam content.\n\n## The 24-hour window\nThe API lets you reply for **24h after the user's last interaction**; after that, **no follow-up unless\nthey re-engage.** Best practice: **compress promo into the first 24h, then move the relationship to\nemail** (→ `email-and-newsletter`).\n\n## The ~12 behaviors that cause ~94% of bans\nTop triggers: (1) **same exact text to >25 recipients/hour** (fingerprint detection — incl. emoji/link\nslugs); (2) **cold/non-opted-in** sends; (3) **>1 external link** per message; (4) **URL shorteners**\n(bit.ly etc. — deboosted/flagged); (5) **unofficial scraping tools**. Also: **report rate >0.6%** →\nauto-review; **opt-out >4%** is a top trigger. Official-API tools = **~27× lower ban risk.** Limits\n(verify-quarterly): 20–50/day new, 50–100 established, 5–15/hr, 1,000 chars; new accounts warm up over\n~30 days.\n\n## Manual warm / partnership outreach\nFor genuine 1:1 outreach, send **manually** in time blocks (each message approved) — \"fully automated\ncold DMs trigger immediate bans.\" **Personalize** (reference something specific → +40% response); no\ngeneric \"Hey!\"; **no link in the first message**; avoid spam words (\"free money\", \"click here\", \"limited\ntime\"); **respect bios** (\"no DMs / email only\"); **partnership disclosures must be public** (comments/\ncaptions), not just DM. Route high-intent to a **human**. Tools (advisory): ManyChat/LinkDM/CreatorFlow/\nPilotDM — **always official Meta API**, never scrapers.\n"
